# 01 - Flashing RGB LED

## Objective

Create the simplest ESP32 program by blinking an LED.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- LED
- 220 Ω resistor
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- digitalWrite()
- delay()
- variables

## Wiring

|   LED   |               ESP32              |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| Anode   | GPIO 23 (through 220 Ω resistor) |
| Cathode | GND                              |

## Expected Result

The LED turns on for one second and turns off for one second continuously.

## What I Learned

- RGB values
- How current flows through an LED
- Why a resistor is required
- How the Arduino loop() function works
- How to properly use variables
- How to use delays properly

## Resources

- ESP32 Documentation
- Arduino Documentation
